+## End each reply with status and asks
+
+Questions and requests scattered through an interleaved reply are easy
+to miss. End every reply that is not a patch with a short summary, so
+the reader sees at a glance where the work stands and what is asked of
+them:
+
+    Objective: <the task you were given>
+    Status: <done, or blocked and on what>
+    Next actions for you:
+    - <what the reader must do, or "none">
+    Information needed from you:
+    - <what you need to know, or "none">
+
+A task you were given ends one of two ways. Either you finished it, or
+you are blocked on something only the reader can provide. If it is
+done, the next actions say what the reader does with the result, such
+as reviewing a posted series. If it is not done, at least one of the
+two lists names what unblocks it. A task that is not done, with "none"
+in both lists, means you stopped without cause. Finish the work
+instead.
+
+Interleaved answers stay where they are. The summary repeats any ask
+made above it, so the reader can act on the summary alone.
+
 ## Read the whole batch before working
 
 When you fetch new mail, read every message in the batch before you
